architecture financial-workbook
  canonical_name FinancialWorkbook
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-lifetime.mjs
  invariant account-change and pagehide events permanently close the current workbook lifetime, abort native transport and workers, clear the private view and require a fresh page read before reopening
  invariant queued native file and record operations check the lifetime before dispatch; a dispatched save may have completed, so its delayed reply cannot rehydrate the closed editor or trigger a retry
  invariant imported files, delayed configuration and initial record reads cannot open a workbook after lifetime invalidation; the shared native store remains the authority and revision owner
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-lifetime.test.mjs verifies one-time cleanup, aborted transport, delayed module refusal and no retry of uncertain saves
  witness scripts/tests/workbook-account-browser.test.mjs exercises native browser account events, held reads, held import worker loading, page lifecycle return, changed-account reload and a delayed real save acknowledgement
  known_gap workbook account cleanup relies on the existing account-change and page lifecycle events; it is not an independent session monitor or server revocation feed
  forbidden_inference aborting a workbook session -> cancellation or rollback of a save already received by the native owner
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-analysis.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-analysis-view.mjs
  invariant sensitivity evaluates two to 15 distinct finite inputs against the same named driver and formula output, including an independently recalculated current baseline
  invariant goal seeking uses a finite bracket, explicit result tolerance and at most 24 bisection steps; calculation errors or unmet residual tolerance produce no solution
  invariant analyses run in the existing isolated scenario worker with a 30 second deadline; a goal result can only create a draft assumption set, followed by the existing preview, adoption and native save flow
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-analysis.test.mjs covers real formula sweeps, baseline and endpoint matches, maximum sweep bounds, invalid results and discontinuous nonconvergence
  witness scripts/tests/workbook-analysis-browser.test.mjs checks native browser analysis, source preservation, explicit goal-set creation and stale result invalidation
  forbidden_inference a sensitivity sweep or bracketed goal match -> model validity, a unique or global optimum, continuity, forecast accuracy or authority to change financial records
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-scenarios.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-scenarios-view.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-evaluate.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-scenario-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-scenario-calculation.mjs
  invariant assumption sets belong to the existing revisioned workbook record; at most 24 named numeric drivers and 24 sets fit a 64 KiB metadata bound
  invariant scenario comparison recalculates the current baseline and candidate through the same Univer evaluator in disposable workers; error, timeout, cancellation and changed workbook or set prevent adoption
  invariant preview does not mutate cells or save records; explicit adoption changes the current draft and Save review retains it through existing native revision and account checks
  invariant machine transaction previews preserve valid assumption sets in the exact native record body
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-scenarios.test.mjs verifies real formula evaluation, source retention, stale preview refusal, driver bounds, set persistence and worker cancellation
  witness scripts/tests/workbook-scenarios-browser.test.mjs operates the actual native package with worker previews, explicit adoption, error refusal, phone reopening, MCP preservation and stale-save refusal
  known_gap assumption sets bind worksheet addresses rather than tracking row movement; changed sheet names or dimensions refuse application, but moved rows require the user to check driver meaning
  forbidden_inference a saved or applied scenario -> forecast validity, financial advice, automatic model optimization or preservation of scenario metadata in XLSX
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-lineage.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-lineage-view.mjs
  invariant formula lineage projects the existing Univer dependency trees for the exact current workbook; ranges remain bounded references, every current formula must be represented, and obsolete inspection results cannot replace a newer edit
  invariant the lineage inspector distinguishes direct and transitive dependents, reads no external sources, changes no cells and preserves original workbook bytes; headless calculation exposes the same optional graph within its worker deadline
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-lineage.test.mjs exercises real formula-engine cross-sheet references, ranges, quoted names, direct and indirect dependents, changed formulas and stale graph refusal
  witness scripts/tests/workbook-lineage-browser.test.mjs inspects the actual native finance editor and follows a formula reference without altering its saved workbook
  forbidden_inference a formula dependency graph -> financial correctness, actual execution of every conditional branch, historical imported-cell lineage or supported external workbook links
  family surface
  domain Finance / Workbook review
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can a person import a financial workbook, edit and recalculate its assumptions, and continue the same source-bearing review with another authorized member of the organization?
  purpose Use the existing ServiceSite renderer and native workspace owners to expose a Univer review instrument, bounded XLSX exchange and revisioned account records without adding a financial ledger or another storage owner.
  internal_calculus Actual ZIP expansion bound before XML parsing
  internal_calculus Supported scalar and formula workbook projection
  internal_calculus Independent formula evaluation with circular-reference and deadline refusal
  internal_calculus Immutable workbook bodies under native workspace revisions
  internal_calculus Pack-declared financial-workbooks family and exact continuation projection
  internal_calculus Configurable transaction column mapping, exact-cent totals and duplicate groups
  internal_calculus Row decisions bound to current content and duplicate-group fingerprints
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-model.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-import.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-import-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-record.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-calculation.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-calculation-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-editor.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-review.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-review-view.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-workspace-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-package.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/workbook_mcp.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-app.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-controller.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-mcp-build.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/workbook.mjs
  source_path scripts/publish_experience_setups.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/workspace-value.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-import.test.mjs verifies original-file retention, cached result replacement, last-row bounds, unsupported content refusal and dishonest ZIP expansion
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-calculation.test.mjs evaluates Books formulas with Univer, edits assumptions, exports and reopens XLSX, refuses circular references and terminates expired calculation workers
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-native.test.mjs exercises real isolated Auth, CMS and WebAddress owners for installation, authorized shared review, large workbook bodies, current role checks, stale saves, account isolation, deactivation and exact continuation
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-material.test.mjs builds the browser bundle through the existing ServiceSite workspace renderer
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-review.test.mjs verifies column mapping, missing amounts, duplicate explanations, stale decision refusal, original source retention and exported decision and account sheets
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-facade.test.mjs verifies real Univer edits clear replaced formulas, preserve formatting, retain literal account text and recalculate dependent cells
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp.test.mjs verifies account MCP operations and manual review continue the same native workbook record with shared validation and formula calculation
  invariant original imported XLSX bytes remain a separately retained source; an exported review is a new file
  invariant imports bound actual decompression to 32 MiB from an 8 MiB archive and refuse encrypted, macro, merged and unsupported formula inputs
  invariant review calculation uses Univer 1.1.0 and explicitly refuses circular references and error cells; a cached value cannot establish recalculation
  invariant workbook JSON bodies use the existing immutable file transport while record metadata remains within the native 256 KiB contract
  invariant account records use the Pack-declared financial-workbooks family and finance-workbook prefix with existing installation, destination, Auth role and CMS revision checks
  invariant old browser v1 records remain readable and subsequent saves use v2 immutable workbook bodies
  invariant package material contains the editor and continuation descriptor, never private workbook fixtures or source documents
  invariant review decisions apply only to the same mapped row content and duplicate group; missing amounts, accounts, descriptions and formula errors prevent marking a row reviewed
  invariant possible duplicate decisions require a note; batches validate all selected fingerprints before replacing decisions
  invariant review decision bodies have the same 8 MiB UTF-8 bound when written and read, including multi-byte notes
  invariant imported-cell comparison shows the original workbook address, not inferred lineage after row insertion or movement
  known_gap browser witnesses cover isolated native Chrome at 1440 and 390 pixels, not every supported browser, complete accessibility, embedded host behavior, or live signed-in acceptance
  known_gap rich text, merged cells, shared formulas, table references, external workbook references and unsupported functions require a broader exchange contract; this is not lossless Excel editing
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-mcp.test.mjs exercises the official MCP Apps bridge with real isolated account services; UI rendering remains unverified
  known_gap the native review record is not yet a ledger reconciliation, posting approval or valuation workflow; the embedded MCP App still needs host and browser verification
  known_gap browser calculation runs within the editor runtime; only the headless calculation path and import worker have process termination deadlines
  forbidden_inference saved or recalculated workbook -> financial correctness, reconciliation completion, authorized posting, payment, audit approval or lossless Excel compatibility
  forbidden_inference passing native HTTP and calculation tests -> a verified browser interface or deployed public demo
  forbidden_inference marking a workbook row reviewed -> authenticated approval, reconciliation, independent source verification or authority to post a transaction
  interacts books-review-enters-financial-workbook
  interacts financial-workbook-uses-native-workspace
  interacts service-site-renders-financial-workbook
  interacts account-mcp-operates-financial-workbook

  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-presentation.css
  witness scripts/tests/workspace_entry_presentation.test.mjs imports an actual illustrative XLSX through its worker, saves with native workspace revisions, reopens supported formulas and preserves exact original bytes at desktop and phone widths
  witness scripts/tests/workspace_entry_presentation.test.mjs exercises transaction mapping, current account totals, duplicate and missing-amount metrics, original-cell inspection, explained duplicate review, native save and reduced motion; the transaction case passed 17 assertions on 2026-10-20
  invariant the import entrance, working toolbar, review filters, inspector and account summary share one scoped stylesheet compiled with the existing Univer editor; presentation does not replace workbook calculation or native storage
  invariant displayed account totals are the existing exact-cent review projection over all mapped rows; awaiting-review rows remain included, missing amounts remain explicit and no currency or ledger posting is inferred
  forbidden_inference an updated preview or styled account total -> completion of a donor finance skill, financial approval or live browser acceptance

interaction books-review-enters-financial-workbook
  source cmd-books
  destination financial-workbook
  relation review-workbook-recalculation
  preserves original review bytes, account labels, transaction values, supported formulas and source worksheet content
  drops cached formula authority and unimplemented Excel features
  forbidden_inference recalculated export -> a validated categorization or posted ledger entry
  invalidates_on Books export columns, formula semantics, SheetJS exchange or Univer runtime changes
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-calculation.test.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/books_xlsx.c
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-model.mjs

interaction financial-workbook-uses-native-workspace
  source financial-workbook
  destination web-address-edge
  relation account-bound-workbook-review
  preserves current session, organization, installed family, native record revision, immutable source and workbook bodies, and exact saved-review continuation
  drops inferred account access, arbitrary storage endpoints and application-owned draft databases
  forbidden_inference installation or a saved review -> permission to post transactions or mutate external financial systems
  invalidates_on native binding, current role, installation state, workbook record schema or editor package changes
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-native.test.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-package.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-record.mjs
  binding scripts/publish_experience_setups.mjs

interaction service-site-renders-financial-workbook
  source service-site
  destination financial-workbook
  relation existing-workspace-section-material
  preserves supplied workbook identity, material route, site theme, workspace layout and shared browser store
  drops any claim that static material has a private account binding
  forbidden_inference a built static workbook page -> account-scoped storage or safe publication of private financial data
  invalidates_on ServiceSite workspace section contract, asset paths, workbook model or runtime changes
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/workbook-material.test.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/workbook-material.mjs
  binding components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/workbook.mjs
